From e3c6341e3118d446889beb4a894df09c783d3ab9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code Review <claude-review@example.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:26:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add real landing page and visual design system
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces a stray leftover 'Diablo 4 theme' in globals.css (blood-red
accents, Cinzel font, glow effects on every element) with an actual
design system, and gives the app a real marketing landing page
instead of the login form sitting at '/'.

Design concept: the name ImmortalQR is the brief — a code that
outlives what it's printed on, because the destination updates
without reprinting. Grounded the look in ink-on-paper permanence
(stamps, plaques) rather than a generic SaaS template:
- Palette: paper white, near-black ink, one antique-brass accent
  (kept out of button text, used only for dividers/focus states/the
  hero graphic, to protect contrast)
- Type: Fraunces (display serif) + Work Sans (body/UI), loaded via
  _document.js
- Signature element: an abstracted, deliberately non-scannable
  QR-module pattern as the hero graphic (src/components/QrGridArt.js)
  — used once, not repeated as decoration
- Flat sections with hairline dividers instead of a shadowed-card kit

Structural changes:
- index.js is now the landing page (hero, 3-feature section, footer
  with Terms/Privacy links); the existing login/register form moved
  to a new login.js, functionally unchanged
- authOptions.js: pages.signIn updated to /login (was '/', which no
  longer has a login form) — this is the one change here that
  affects behavior, not just styling
- src/components/Nav.js: shared header for dashboard/settings
  (brand, settings link, sign out), replacing duplicated ad hoc
  headers on each page
- dashboard.js, settings.js, forgot-password.js, reset-password.js,
  terms.js, privacy.js, QrTable.js, RequireAuth.js: restyled with
  the shared design system, logic unchanged
- QrTable: wrapped in an overflow-x scroll container so 5 columns
  don't break on mobile

Accessibility: verified contrast ratios against the new palette;
darkened --ink-faint (8A8F97 -> 676B72, 3.03:1 -> 4.98:1) after it
failed WCAG AA for the small text it's used on (timestamps, empty
state, footer). Focus-visible outlines added globally. Reduced
motion respected for the hero graphic's entrance animation.
